  ],
  "preconditions": [
    "Owned native Linux temporary roots and canonical project/document/release bundles generated from native model fixtures; original endpoint proofs and configuration parent context. Synthetic reviews are fixture inputs, not real human approvals."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Extract verified owned bytes through direct, CLI, structured-request and registry routes into missing or empty targets; compare original payload and manifest bytes, reopen complete projects and reproduce their bundle.",
    "Preserve partial configuration and review proof files separately; reject complete-project loading and full export, including after root-manifest removal while the retained bootstrap proof remains.",
    "Reject foreign target contents and invalid, linked, changed or hash-mismatched inputs before mutation. Inject native preparation/publication failures and verify original target preservation.",
    "Resume the exact verified payload from a proven durable prefix; recheck completed receipts and reject altered or foreign inventories without overwriting.",
    "15.e.R uses native process hard exits at durable preparation, every project publication unit and completion; validates exact replay input and actual inodes, checks hostile ZIP vectors before writes, and preserves conflicts under I/O failures, changed journals, links, replaced targets, concurrent foreign writes and changed input. A configuration published before bootstrap completion cannot open a complete-project reader."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "`specroad bundle extract <FILE> --output <DIR>` MUSS ausschließlich verifizierte Bundles unter den Pfad-, Ziel- und harten Sicherheitsregeln aus Kapitel 10.16, 11.7 und Anhang E extrahieren; weiche Arbeitsbudgets folgen Anhang O.",
    "scope": "15.e.W/R native Linux journaled extraction of currently verifiable project and partial bundles. Existing BootstrapTree owns no-replace publication, configuration-last ordering, rollback and retained proof. Complete projects reopen and remain subject to normal write gates. Partials are conservatively excluded from the complete-project reader until 15.f; no context promotion or implicit rehydration. No cross-platform, unimplemented portable receipts, authenticity, full semantic validation or release claim. R guards the original input and exact root namespace at every publication boundary and after receipt retention. Interrupted replay retains its proven prefix and never reports success after a fault; fresh ordinary failures restore the owned original state or retain the complete published root. Unverifiable/foreign remnants are retained as conflicts."
  },
